# Every text file is LF, both in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Without `eol=lf`, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as
# CRLF. The committed content is unaffected (git normalizes on the way in), but
# `npm run format:check` then fails on the whole tree, because .prettierrc pins
# endOfLine: "lf" — formatting drift that only exists on one developer's disk.
# It also keeps shell scripts and Dockerfiles runnable when built from a
# Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
